            "verdict": "benign",
            "normalizedStatus": "clean",
            "analysis": "Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: clawsec-suite\nVersion: 0.1.6\n\nThe clawsec-suite bundle is a security management tool for the OpenClaw ecosystem designed to monitor for and mitigate risks from malicious or vulnerable skills. It implements robust defensive measures, including Ed25519 cryptographic signature verification for its advisory feed, SHA-256 checksum validation for artifacts, and a strict HTTPS domain allowlist (restricting egress to prompt.security and github.com). The suite enforces a 'double-confirmation' policy for risky operations, requiring explicit user approval before installing flagged skills or removing existing ones. All persistent components, such as the advisory guardian hook and periodic cron jobs, are disclosed via preflight reviews in the setup scripts (setup_advisory_hook.mjs and setup_advisory_cron.mjs). No evidence of data exfiltration, unauthorized execution, or malicious prompt injection was found.",
